>root@aix1.uottawa.ca protesting about Jean-Serge Gagnon's illegal and
>unethical abuse of our newsgroup and requesting that he BE
>DISCONNECTED FROM THE NET IMMEDIATELY AND PERMANENTLY.

Pete Hickey (Pete@mudhead.uottawa.CA) writes:

>Its been done.  Please don't cause us any more grief by complaining.

Expulsion from the Net permanently seems a overly harsh, at least
without some due process first. I hope you respected the accused's
academic freedom and due process rights, including:
     - no punishment before a hearing (although access could be
         suspended in the interim if you have good reason to think
         there is danger to safety or property).
     - a fair hearing following an established due process procedure
     - (maybe) no public announcement of the punishment (In the U.S.,
         public annoucenments with respect to student punishments are
         illegal.)

Imposing harsh summary punishments may be a good way for a university
to end public complaints but it is a poor way for a university to
achieve justice.

- Carl
